{
 "about": "Sets whose status is DRAFT, ARCHIVED, or absent (the upload carries no status field). The expected reading: only ACTIVE sets take part, and a set created without a status is DRAFT; round 24 and 25 found a nested INACTIVE set applying and a top-level one not. At the top, the set's one ALLOW rule decides under each algorithm: true if the set applies, false if not. Nested, the parent is ACTIVE and the nested set is the only child that decides: true or false tells whether it applies. Each case asks check/resource and check/filter.",
